      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Express $2\\cos^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)-2\\sin^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&2\\cos^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)-2\\sin^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=2\\left(\\cos^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x-\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=168^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot 168^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(336^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\left(\\cos^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)\\right)&=2\\cos\\left(336^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
